<title>UK: EIB sets 500 billion lire five-year bond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 500 billion lire five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Credito Italiano and Banco di Roma.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    500 BLN LIRE  COUPON     6.20	MATURITY    05.MAR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.706   PAY DATE    05.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.75	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS **</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES    **GENERAL SALES LIMITS OF EIB WITH SPECIFICATIONS</p>
<p>		FOR ITALY ONLY.</p>
<p>		LAUNCHED OFF ISSUERS DEBT ISSUANCE PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
